2) Changing the method to  method = "Nelder-Mead" produced the same issues as nlm where the maximization values jumped dramatically and never recovered.

3) including link= list(D="identity") without typsize argument resulted in large fluctuations in the maximization values as well resulting in the same density estimate for each session and failed to estimate variance.

Warning messages:
1 to 11  In f(x, ...) : invalid density <= 0
12: In secr.fit(SC_CH, mask = mask, sessioncov = data.frame(year = c(2006,  ... :
  possible maximization error: nlm returned code 3. See ?nlm
13: In secr.fit(SC_CH, mask = mask, sessioncov = data.frame(year = c(2006,  ... :
  at least one variance calculation failed

3) including both link= list(D="identity") and typsize argument resulted in similar density estimates for all years (unlikely to be true), lcl of 0 and large ucl. With the following warning messages:

Warning messages:
1: In f(x, ...) : invalid density <= 0
